-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §11.0.2: the IN roll is read ONCE, for the whole
-- group, before there is any member to speak of, so it may not mention the
-- member it is drawing. The member variable is deliberately out of scope
-- there, exactly as it is out of scope in a join line's WITHIN, so this is a
-- check-time error and not a run-time refusal.
--
-- Measured limit, 2026-09-08: the rejection arrives as the generic "could not
-- find a definition", the same wording the join line's restriction gets. A
-- dedicated diagnostic is not built.
--
-- The older inferred spelling cannot be caught here — the WHO condition does
-- bind the member, legitimately, for its other conjuncts — so there the same
-- mistake is a run-time refusal instead. Its witness is
-- jl4/examples/ok/every/run-roll.l4's `circular`.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Tenant HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign HAS signer IS AN Actor

GIVEN p IS AN Actor
GIVETH A LIST OF Actor
peersOf MEANS LIST p

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`roll mentions the member` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN (peersOf t) MUST Sign (EXACTLY t) WITHIN 14
